{"id":"5ddc9021c037117b","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-uniform-integrability.md","title":"Uniform Integrability","display":"df-uniform-integrability — Uniform Integrability","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-uniform-integrability","aliases":["58-df-uniform-integrability","Uniform Integrability"],"display":"df-uniform-integrability — Uniform Integrability","depends_on":["[[58-df-probability]]","[[58-df-measurable-function]]","[[58-df-measurable-space]]","[[58-df-integral]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-uniform-integrability"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-uniform-integrability</span><span>Uniform Integrability</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-uniform-integrability — Uniform Integrability"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5e0db065132180df\" href=\"?note=5e0db065132180df\" title=\"58-df-probability\">58-df-probability</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"58-df-measurable-function\">58-df-measurable-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"7f96c502a4a99a46\" href=\"?note=7f96c502a4a99a46\" title=\"58-df-measurable-space\">58-df-measurable-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"58-df-integral\">58-df-integral</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P\\in V\">\\(\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P\\in V\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathscr F)\">\\(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathscr F)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"5e0db065132180df\" href=\"?note=5e0db065132180df\" title=\"58-df-probability\">58-df-probability</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathscr X\\subseteq\\mathbb C^\\Omega\">\\(\\mathscr X\\subseteq\\mathbb C^\\Omega\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\)</span> (measurable-function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"58-df-measurable-function\">58-df-measurable-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B_+\">\\(\\mathcal B_+\\)</span> is the Borel sigma-algebra on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[0,\\infty]\">\\([0,\\infty]\\)</span>, with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+)\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|f|\\coloneqq\\{\\langle x,|f(x)|\\rangle:x\\in\\Omega\\}\">\\(|f|\\coloneqq\\{\\langle x,|f(x)|\\rangle:x\\in\\Omega\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g_{f,K}\\coloneqq\\{\\langle x,|f(x)|\\mathbf1_{\\{|f|&gt;K\\}}(x)\\rangle:x\\in\\Omega\\}\">\\(g_{f,K}\\coloneqq\\{\\langle x,|f(x)|\\mathbf1_{\\{|f|&gt;K\\}}(x)\\rangle:x\\in\\Omega\\}\\)</span> are the pointwise nonnegative function graphs</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{UI}_S(\\mathscr X;\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P)\">\\(\\operatorname{UI}_S(\\mathscr X;\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}uniform\\text{-}integrability}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{UI}_S(\\mathscr X;\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathscr F)\n\\land\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+)\n\\land\\mathscr X\\subseteq\\mathbb C^\\Omega\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall f\\in\\mathscr X\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(f;(\\Omega,\\mathscr F),(\\mathbb C,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C)))\n\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(|f|;(\\Omega,\\mathscr F),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\n\\land\\int_\\Omega|f|\\,d\\mathbb P&lt;\\infty\n\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists K\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall f\\in\\mathscr X\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g_{f,K};(\\Omega,\\mathscr F),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\n\\land\\int_\\Omega g_{f,K}\\,d\\mathbb P&lt;\\varepsilon\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}uniform\\text{-}integrability}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{UI}_S(\\mathscr X;\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathscr F)\n\\land\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+)\n\\land\\mathscr X\\subseteq\\mathbb C^\\Omega\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall f\\in\\mathscr X\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(f;(\\Omega,\\mathscr F),(\\mathbb C,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C)))\n\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(|f|;(\\Omega,\\mathscr F),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\n\\land\\int_\\Omega|f|\\,d\\mathbb P&lt;\\infty\n\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists K\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall f\\in\\mathscr X\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g_{f,K};(\\Omega,\\mathscr F),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\n\\land\\int_\\Omega g_{f,K}\\,d\\mathbb P&lt;\\varepsilon\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The absolute-value and tail graphs are explicitly required to lie in the nonnegative measurable domain on which the registered Lebesgue integral is defined.</li>\n<li>Uniform integrability: family bounded in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^1\">\\(L^1\\)</span> and equi-absolutely continuous</li>\n<li>Vitali convergence: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal{F}\">\\(\\mathcal{F}\\)</span> UI + convergence in probability <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\implies\">\\(\\implies\\)</span> convergence in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^1\">\\(L^1\\)</span></li>\n<li>de la Vallée-Poussin gives an equivalent uniform bound by a superlinear convex function.</li>\n<li>Applications: martingale convergence, limit theorems in probability</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples</li>\n<li>Williams, Probability with Martingales</li>\n<li>Kallenberg, Foundations of Modern Probability</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-probability","status":"resolved","id":"5e0db065132180df","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-probability]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measurable-function","status":"resolved","id":"bbbec05fde1d3b01","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measurable-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measurable-space","status":"resolved","id":"7f96c502a4a99a46","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measurable-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-integral","status":"resolved","id":"4884f45058a56aac","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-integral]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-probability","status":"resolved","id":"5e0db065132180df","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P\\in V$ with $\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathscr F)$ (see [[58-df-probability]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measurable-function","status":"resolved","id":"bbbec05fde1d3b01","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathscr X\\subseteq\\mathbb C^\\Omega$ and $\\mathrm{Measurable}_S$ (measurable-function predicate, see [[58-df-measurable-function]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathscr F)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathscr X\\subseteq\\mathbb C^\\Omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B_+","display":false},{"tex":"[0,\\infty]","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+)","display":false},{"tex":"|f|\\coloneqq\\{\\langle x,|f(x)|\\rangle:x\\in\\Omega\\}","display":false},{"tex":"g_{f,K}\\coloneqq\\{\\langle x,|f(x)|\\mathbf1_{\\{|f|>K\\}}(x)\\rangle:x\\in\\Omega\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{UI}_S(\\mathscr X;\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}uniform\\text{-}integrability}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{UI}_S(\\mathscr X;\\Omega,\\mathscr F,\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathscr F)\n\\land\\mathrm{MeasurableSpace}_S([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+)\n\\land\\mathscr X\\subseteq\\mathbb C^\\Omega\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land\\forall f\\in\\mathscr X\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(f;(\\Omega,\\mathscr F),(\\mathbb C,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C)))\n\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(|f|;(\\Omega,\\mathscr F),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\n\\land\\int_\\Omega|f|\\,d\\mathbb P<\\infty\n\\Bigr)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\exists K\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\n\\forall f\\in\\mathscr X\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g_{f,K};(\\Omega,\\mathscr F),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\n\\land\\int_\\Omega g_{f,K}\\,d\\mathbb P<\\varepsilon\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"L^1","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal{F}","display":false},{"tex":"\\implies","display":false},{"tex":"L^1","display":false}],"bytes":2603,"backlinks":[{"id":"59ee0c08880a79d3","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1347","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-uniform-integrability.md|58-df-uniform-integrability]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["5e0db065132180df","bbbec05fde1d3b01","7f96c502a4a99a46","4884f45058a56aac"]}